// ============================================================================
// frft_hunt.kn — TurboKain 22: Coherent Fast Fractional Fourier Transform (FrFT)
// Chirp Matched Filter on Baseband / Voltage Slices (Ozaktas / Pei-Ding O(N log N))
//
// Theoretical Foundation:
//   Standard incoherent drift searches (drift_hunt, TurboSETI) sum power along
//   linear paths in 2D time-frequency waterfalls, suffering a sqrt(N) SNR loss.
//   The Fractional Fourier Transform X_alpha(u) rotates the time-frequency plane
//   by angle alpha = a * pi/2, mapping linear frequency chirps mu = -cot(alpha)*fs^2/N
//   directly into coherent Dirac-delta impulse tones in the fractional domain u.
//
// Mathematical Engine:
//   Fast discrete FrFT computes continuous parameter rotations in O(N_alpha * N log N):
//     1. Pre-chirp multiply:   x1[n] = x[n] * exp(-j*pi*(n - N/2)^2/N * tan(alpha/2))
//     2. Chirp convolution:   x2 = IFFT_2N( FFT_2N(x1) .* FFT_2N(g) )
//                              where g[m] = exp(j*pi*(m - N)^2/N * csc(alpha))
//     3. Post-chirp multiply:  y[k] = x2[k + N/2] * exp(-j*pi*(k - N/2)^2/N * tan(alpha/2))
//                              normalized by 1 / sqrt(N * |sin(alpha)|) for Parseval unitarity.
//
// Robust Statistics:
//   * Running median background (w=101) with converge med100 (insertion vs quickselect).
//   * Median Absolute Deviation (MAD) with G5 MAD-floor (1e-9) to prevent division blowup.
//   * Non-max suppression +-3 bins (top 25 per alpha).
//   * Cross-alpha deduplication with TIE-PREFERS-RATE-0 (defaults to a=1.0 ordinary FT).
//
// Laws & Semantics:
//   * law alpha_in_range: bounds rotation angles away from singular asymptotes.
//   * law parseval_ok: verifies energy conservation sum(|y|^2) == sum(|x|^2) +- 2%.
//   * law frft_hit_ok: gates signal significance and non-quarantine status.
//
// Exit codes: 0 searched, 1 help / prove FAIL, 2 error.
// ============================================================================

